(573751, 59302, 772, '<td valign="top">Shallow depth of field here is ok.  The image doesn''t seem to strike me in any particular way.  There is a lot of color here that seems to clash.  The background is strong... possibly overpowering your subject(s).  It may also be useful to upset the ''balance'' somehow... After continuing to look, the film canisters in this image don''t serve much of any purpose other than to show shallow depth of field?  You may find it useful to incorporate subject strength with the challeng topic :)</td>', 'Shallow depth of field here is ok.  The image doesn''t seem to strike me in any particular way.  There is a lot of color here that seems to clash.  The background is strong... possibly overpowering your subject(s).  It may also be useful to upset the ''balance'' somehow... After continuing to look, the film canisters in this image don''t serve much of any purpose other than to show shallow depth of field?  You may find it useful to incorporate subject strength with the challeng topic :)', '2004-02-09 18:14:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(573752, 59306, 772, '<td valign="top">This is a nice ''product'' style photo.  The lighting is excellent.  The red contrasts nicely with your white background and surface.  I think this photo would also do well with a slightly lower camera angle and maybe a slight rotation of the car to create some more diagonal punch in the frame.  As for shallow depth of field, I don''t see any.</td>', 'This is a nice ''product'' style photo.  The lighting is excellent.  The red contrasts nicely with your white background and surface.  I think this photo would also do well with a slightly lower camera angle and maybe a slight rotation of the car to create some more diagonal punch in the frame.  As for shallow depth of field, I don''t see any.', '2004-02-09 18:16:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(573754, 58847, 772, '<td valign="top">I like the perspective of this shot... It makes me think the dog is stalking something in the snow...  The dog is in a bit of an uncomfortable position in the frame for me though.  Maybe higher or lower would work better.  This shot also feels like it should be horizontal rather than vertical.  The shallow depth of field didn''t seem to work out very well here either... just the opposite has occurred... everything seems to be in field...</td>', 'I like the perspective of this shot... It makes me think the dog is stalking something in the snow...  The dog is in a bit of an uncomfortable position in the frame for me though.  Maybe higher or lower would work better.  This shot also feels like it should be horizontal rather than vertical.  The shallow depth of field didn''t seem to work out very well here either... just the opposite has occurred... everything seems to be in field...', '2004-02-09 18:19:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(573756, 58966, 772, '<td valign="top">The shallow depth of field worked out in this shot, but the part of the image that is in focus is insignificant in terms of the entire subject.  The lighting is also a bit inappropriated to create a visually appealing image.</td>', 'The shallow depth of field worked out in this shot, but the part of the image that is in focus is insignificant in terms of the entire subject.  The lighting is also a bit inappropriated to create a visually appealing image.', '2004-02-09 18:20:16.000000', NULL, 1),
